CI/CD Interview Series (Part 1): GitHub Actions — 10 Must-Know Questions for Every DevOps Engineer!

💡 Preparing for DevOps or Cloud interviews?
Here’s a crisp, practical Q&A guide to master GitHub Actions — straight to the point, no fluff!

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 🧠 1️⃣ What’s CI/CD in GitHub Actions?

CI → Builds & tests your code automatically when you push changes.
CD → Deploys that tested code to your servers or cloud.
All this magic happens through YAML workflow files that run on GitHub’s runners.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 📁 2️⃣ Where do workflow files live?

Inside your repo → `.github/workflows/`
File type → `.yml` or `.yaml`
(👉 GitHub ignores them if they’re elsewhere!)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### ⚙️ 3️⃣ What triggers a workflow?

* `push` → When you push new commits
* `pull_request` → When someone opens a PR
* `schedule` → Run at specific times (like cron)
* `workflow_dispatch` → Manual trigger button

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 🧩 4️⃣ Workflow vs Job vs Step — What’s the difference?

* Workflow = Entire automation (1 YAML file)
* Job = Main task (can run in parallel)
* Step = Individual commands inside a job

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### ⚡ 5️⃣ What are Actions?

Reusable code blocks that save you scripting time!
✅ `actions/checkout` → Pulls your repo
✅ `actions/cache` → Speeds up builds
✅ Community actions → Deploy to AWS, Azure, Docker Hub & more

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 🖥️ 6️⃣ What are Runners?

The machines executing your workflows.

* GitHub-hosted: Free, clean, auto-updated
* Self-hosted: Your own server = more control + no timeouts

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 🔒 7️⃣ How to manage secrets safely?

❌ Never hard-code passwords!
✅ Use GitHub Secrets: `${{ secrets.API_KEY }}`
✅ Use `${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}` for GitHub auth
✅ Add manual approvals for production deploys

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### ⚡ 8️⃣ What does `actions/cache` do?

It stores downloaded packages so builds run faster.
Example: npm/pip modules → cached once, reused later.
⏱ Build time drops from 10 min to 2 min!

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 🧱 9️⃣ How to protect the main branch?

✅ Make CI checks mandatory
✅ Require tests & build to pass before merge
✅ Add review rules for production repos

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 🚀 🔟 How to organize your pipeline?

Simple & structured: Test → Build → Deploy
1️⃣ Run unit tests & lint checks
2️⃣ If pass ✅ → Build the app
3️⃣ Then deploy to server or cloud

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

### 💡 Pro Tips

✅ Use caching to save time & cost
✅ Split workflows by purpose (test, deploy)
✅ Use matrix testing for multiple versions
✅ Add manual approvals for prod deploys
✅ Keep YAMLs clean & readable
